over the past few weeks apple's new m1  max have been impressing not only apple  fans  but also people who've been using  windows computers for years  with the game changing battery life  being the main advantage so far  linus tech tips finally gave the m1  macbooks an in-depth review  and in their battery life test the m1  13-inch macbook pro  managed to get over 20 hours of battery  life  while the latest dell xps 13 got just  over  12 hours that's an 8 hour difference  and on top of that the m1 is actually  faster  cooler and quieter so to everyone's  surprise  linus actually recommended both the  macbook  air and the pro despite his dumpster  fire of an announcement video  but i don't blame him because even i  didn't expect  rosetta x86 app translation to work  so incredibly well one thing's for sure  though the m1 max  definitely have his curiosity but next  year's  m1x 16-inch macbook pro  will have his attention in this video  i'm gonna take a look at the leaks  surrounding that upcoming 16-inch  macbook  and i'll break down the changes we  should realistically  expect including the performance jump  with the new m1x chip so let's get  started  from all of the leaks we've been seeing  over the past few months  there are two things that we absolutely  know will happen for sure  the 16-inch pro will come with a new  mini led display  and it's going to come with a more  powerful m series apple silicon chip  which i personally think will be called  the m1x chip but before i get into both  of those features  i want to talk about something that we  don't really know for sure  just yet and this one thing will change  everything else  way back in july the reliable apple  analyst  minshikuo said that the first r mac  would be a 13.3 inch macbook pro  shipping before the end of the year  without any sort of design  changes and he was right within that  same investor note  he claimed that two redesigned macbook  pros would be coming  in 2021 including both a 14  and 16 inch macbook pro way later in  december  he said that these two macbook pros will  have mini led displays  and they'll have an all new form factor  design  now the big question is what does all  new form factor mean  in reality the current 16-inch macbook  pro only came out in 2019  with thinner bezels it already came with  updated studio quality microphones  and a new six speaker system how much  more  could they change it well apple could go  all out  and drastically update the design  potentially changing the display  to have rounded corners just like an  ipad pro  and that might actually make sense since  mac os big sur  now features rounded windows or for  example  they could change the macbook exterior  into a flat slab of metal  like the ipad pro but that would require  the body itself  to get thinner or else it's going to  look way too thick  and how could they possibly do that well  if you think about it  the switch to an all-in-one apple  silicon chip  means that the logic board no longer  needs to be as large  just look at the inside of the new m1  mac mini  the logic board is hilariously small the  power supply  has been completely unchanged and it's  overkill for the m1 chip  the fan is also overkill because it  rarely ever spins up  so in reality apple can shrink down all  of those components  on the 16 macbook pro leaving much more  room  for everything else including the  battery pack  so realistically apple could and should  completely redesign the form factor to  take advantage of the space savings  that they can get with the new chips  therefore making the body thinner  on top of that they don't even need to  keep the same  100 watt hour battery pack because of  how little power  these new apple silicon chips take that  100 watt hour battery pack is 71.82  percent larger  than the one in the 13 inch m1 macbook  pro  and based on linus review the m1 pro  got over 20 hours of battery life  so even if you factor in the higher  resolution and display  size of the 16 inch model the battery  life is going to be insane  if apple keeps the 100 watt hour battery  pack  like potentially 30 hours or more  of battery life and here's something  very interesting  the battery in the 13 inch m1 macbook  pro  is only 16.6 percent larger  than the battery pack in the 13-inch  macbook air  but somehow it was able to get an extra  seven hours of battery life in linus's  test  so imagine how much battery life you'll  get  on top of the 13 inch pro from a 71.82  larger battery and the six inch pro now  i know that there are more  factors than that so let's get into the  new mini led display  based on testing done by light science  and applications  mini led consumes less power  than oled and based on testing done by  notebook check  oled should generally consume less power  than  lcd unless you're constantly viewing  over 50  white on your display so in most cases  the new mini led display will help save  battery life on the new 16 inch macbook  pro  on top of the gains from the larger  battery  so realistically apple could easily  shrink down the battery  and make the 16-inch macbook pro thinner  overall  now if you're not familiar with mini led  technology  let me explain how it works for starters  it still uses an lcd panel  which is safe from the burn-in issues  that come with oled displays  the main difference is that instead of  using one huge  led backlight like on an lcd display  mini led  uses hundreds or thousands of small led  backlights  that can be locally controlled and  completely turned off  when displaying black this leads to  excellent contrast  colors and dynamic range similar to an  oled display  this is actually exactly how apple's pro  display xdr  works the only reason it's not called  a mini led display is because the leds  aren't small enough to be technically  called mini because of the huge  32 inch display size now one of the  other benefits of mini led  is that the entire display is actually  thinner  than an lcd display because of that  apple could easily upgrade the webcam to  a 1080p  webcam especially if they're already  gonna redesign the body  or there's even a chance that apple  could go all  out and use the extra space to add face  id  and believe it or not 9-5 mac discovered  mentions of face id in one of the betas  of mac os big sur  so this could actually be happening now  the last thing i want to talk about  is the new m1x chip that will be going  into the 16 inch pro  way back in april it was reported that  apple will be using a 12  core 5 nanometer arm chip in a 2021  macbook and since the m1 has 8 cores  it totally makes sense that the m1x will  be  that 12 core chip that they were talking  about basically  it's gonna have the same four efficiency  cores but it's gonna have  double the amount of performance course  so before i get into the performance  numbers that we should expect  i wanna touch on the battery life for  the most basic  and simple tasks the 16 inch will still  be using  the four efficiency cores to run them  and for watching videos  that is actually handled by the hardware  video decoders  so battery consumption won't go up at  all  and that's how we could potentially see  a 30 hour  battery life figure but in terms of  performance tasks  we can actually calculate the  performance usage  based on the m1 chip's power consumption  under full sustained load  in cinebench r23 the m1 used a total of  14.3 watts  with 13 watts used by the ford  performance cores  and just 1.3 watts used by the  efficiency course  so if the 16 inch gets a 12 core m1x  chip  we can double the power usage of the  four performance cores  and end up with a total of 27.3 watts  under full load and then if we compare  that number  to the power usage of the current intel  i9  16 inch pro it's almost two times more  efficient which is mind-blowing but wait  it gets a whole lot better when we begin  to estimate the performance of the m1x  16-inch macbook pro the current m1 chip  managed to get a score of 7 700 in  cinebench r23  so let's try to break that score down  the four efficiency cores used 1.3 watts  of power  which is about 10 of the power of the  four high performance cores  so if we take the simple route of  dividing that 7700 score in cinebench  by 10 we end up with 700 of that score  coming from the efficiency course and 7  000  from the performance course so if we  assume that the 16 inch pro will get  eight performance cores  that are not gonna throttle because of  efficiency  and the larger cooling system we should  be getting a total score  of 14 700 and cinebench r23  which basically outperforms the 12  core mac pro and that is just insane  that level of performance in a base  16-inch macbook pro  is absolutely unheard of and it's gonna  happen  while using less battery than before and  then if we take a look at the graphics  side  we're expecting the m1x to come packing  a 16 core  gpu so if we double the geek mesh 5  metal score  we got with the m1's 8 core gpu we end  up with around  45 000 points in metal that means that  the m1x's integrated graphics  is going to outperform the absolute best  5600m graphics in the current 16 inch  macbook pro  and if you didn't already know that's  currently  an 800 upgrade option but keep in mind  that the m1x ship will be coming  into the base model 16-inch macbook pro  so if we compare that to the base intel  model  you'll be getting almost double the  graphics performance  and all of that is just looking at raw  performance  if you factor in optimization and  efficiency improvements  from the new unified architecture the  performance is going to be  absolutely insane for example the  current m1 chip  already outperforms the 12 core mac pro  in xcode programming so imagine  the m1x basically what i'm trying to  tell you  is that the 16 inch m1x macbook pro  is gonna blow people's minds it's not  only going to cause  a massive wave of windows laptop users  to switch to the mac but it's literally  going to put the entire computing  industry  into a panic there's going to be a gold  rush of laptop manufacturers  switching to arm-based chips and we'll  start to see announcements  from intel and amd saying that they're  working on  arm chips of their own that are gonna be  going into thin and light laptops  so basically the six inch pro will blow  your mind  and if you're interested in spending  twenty four hundred dollars or more  and you're willing to wait up to half a  year then i would definitely wait  for the m1x pro if this video was  helpful go ahead and tap the like button  and click the circle above to subscribe  definitely check out one of those two  videos right there  thank you for watching and we'll see you  in the next video  you
 

